	// kept: it ends with END_REASON_CANCELLED, and GetJob and ListJobs return
	// it. A job whose command has not started ends at once, and the answer
	// carries the end; a job whose command runs ends once its host has stopped
	// it, and WaitJob waits for that end. Every execution in the job is
	// cancelled. A call for a job that has ended changes nothing and returns
	// the job as it is. An unknown ID fails with NOT_FOUND.
	CancelJob(context.Context, *connect.Request[workspacev1.CancelJobRequest]) (*connect.Response[workspacev1.CancelJobResponse], error)
	// WaitJob blocks until the job is in one of the states asked for or the
	// bound passes, whichever is first, and returns the job as it then is.
	// Passing the bound is not an error: reached is false, and the caller asks
	// again. The server may wait less than the bound asked for.
